**Do this:** here is a wave, in SI units (y and x in metres, t in seconds):

$ y = {exA}·sin(2π(t/{exT} − x/{exLam}))

Lay it on top of the booklet form y = A·sin(2π(t/T − x/λ)) and match the numbers:

- the number **in front** is the amplitude: **A = {exA} m**;
- the number **under t** is the period: **T = {exT} s**, so **f = 1/T = {exF} Hz**;
- the number **under x** is the wavelength: **λ = {exLam} m**;
- the **wave speed** follows: **v = λ/T = f·λ = {exV} m/s**.

That is all the information in the wave. Now try it the other way round.
